  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved food and livelihood security in Bangladesh (Caritas Bangladesh)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project is part of a programme in which four Bangladeshi partners are collaborating together in order to address food and livelihood insecurity, which were identified as the key problems in Bagerhat district.  The partners hold regular meetings and build up linkages with other networks through which monitoring information, reviews, evaluations and experiences can be shared.  Caritas Bangladesh is focusing on activities relating to sustainable agriculture and alternative livelihoods.  This includes training in organic farming methods for rice and vegetable cultivation; tree plantation; supporting the role of women in agriculture; and strengthening people&#x2019;s organisations. Caritas is also supporting advocacy initiatives through its membership of Caritas Asia.</narrative>
  </description>
